milehigh bundles and uses open data and open-source software. Thank you to all of them.

Bundled data (internal/data, regenerated by tools/gendata.py from tools/source)
  - Airports, airlines and aircraft types: OpenFlights (https://openflights.org/data),
    Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
  - Additional and updated airports: OurAirports (https://ourairports.com/data/), public domain,
    as curated for Skyline.
  - Country outlines: Natural Earth 1:50m admin-0 (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/), public domain.
  - Route index (which flight numbers fly between two airports): Virtual Radar Server's
    standing data (https://github.com/vradarserver/standing-data), CC0, as built for Skyline.

Online services (used only when you ask: live position, weather, route lookup, schedules)
  - adsbdb (https://www.adsbdb.com/), open source: routes by flight number.
  - adsb.lol (https://adsb.lol/), ODbL: live aircraft positions.
  - Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com/), CC BY 4.0: weather forecasts.
  - AeroDataBox (https://aerodatabox.com/): schedules and delays, only with your own key.

Libraries
  - Bubble Tea, Bubbles, Lip Gloss by Charm (https://charm.sh), MIT.
  - Their dependencies (termenv, go-runewidth, uniseg, golang.org/x/*…), MIT/BSD/Apache-2.0.
  - Packages are built with GoReleaser (https://goreleaser.com), MIT.
